  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Day unto day uttereth speech, and night unto night sheweth knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "There is no speech nor language, where their voice is not heard.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Which is as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber, and rejoiceth as a strong man to run a race.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "His going forth is from the end of the heaven, and his circuit unto the ends of it: and there is nothing hid from the heat thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "The law of the LORD is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of the LORD is sure, making wise the simple.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The statutes of the LORD are right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the LORD is pure, enlightening the eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring for ever: the judgments of the LORD are true and righteous altogether.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "More to be desired are they than gold, yea, than much fine gold: sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Who can understand his errors? cleanse thou me from secret faults.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous sins; let them not have dominion over me: then shall I be upright, and I shall be innocent from the great transgression.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:19:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 19:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:19:14"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
